>> title: Raspberry Oat Bars
>> category: Bars & Brownies
>> tags: raspberry, oats, jam, dessert, oven
>> servings: 9
>> time: 1 hr
>> step.4: press two thirds into the pan, reserve the rest
>> step.6: spread filling, top with the reserved crumble

Preheat the #oven{} to 375°F (190°C).

Line an #8x8-in pan{} with parchment.

Rub @cold unsalted butter{1/2%cup}(115 g) into @all-purpose flour{1%cup}(130 g), @rolled oats{1%cup}(90 g), @light brown sugar{1/2%cup}(100 g), @baking powder{1/2%tsp}(2 g), @table salt{1/4%tsp}(1.5 g).

Press two thirds of @&(~1)crumble{} firmly into the pan, keeping the rest back.

Stir @raspberry jam{3/4%cup}(240 g), @fresh raspberries{1%cup}(125 g), @cornstarch{2%tsp}(6 g), @lemon juice{1%tsp}(5 mL) together.

Spread @&(~1)raspberry filling{} over @&(~2)crumb base{}, then scatter the reserved crumble over the top.

Bake @&(~1)bars{} at 375°F for ~{35%min}.
